Build artefacts under `build/` (including `file-toto.exe` / `test_core.exe` on
Windows) are gitignored. Directories stay in the repo via `build/.gitkeep` and
`build/tests/.gitkeep`.

## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
./build/file-toto --version
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/file-toto
make clean && make && make test
./build/file-toto --version
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`build/file-toto` or
`build/file-toto.exe`). Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`**. 
Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL load order). 
Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- `classify_content()` is `static inline` in `file_toto.h` when feasible —
  compiled into identify and each test TU; magic table data may live in
  `file_toto_magic.c` and be linked only where needed.
- Tests **do not** link `src/main.c`, `src/file_toto_identify.c`, or
  `src/file_toto_cli.c`.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
- Debug binary is linked in one step from sources with `CFLAGS_DEBUG` (does not
  reuse release `.o` files).
